# Context discipline

Law: agent spend is dominated by re-sent reads. Navigation is by **search**,
then **windows**, not whole files.

**Search before read.** `grep` with line numbers or semantic search. Open only
~150 lines around the hit (`offset`/`limit`). Never read a file over ~300
lines or any doc in full unless the task is to edit that whole file. Prefer
the named owner's section (e.g. `TOPBAR.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md` §) over the
whole doc. Put known `path:line` targets in subagent prompts. Delegate
open-ended “where is X?” to a cheap scout that returns **file:line only**.

```text
// BAD — 10k-line board.rs loaded because the question was vague
Read board.rs (full)

// GOOD — hit then window
Grep "finish_draw" apps/slate/src/app/board.rs → Read offset 6400 limit 150
```
